ACPI video brightness keys

The brightness keys on many laptops (Dell XPS 15 9560 and others) do not
send PS/2 scancodes. They only generate ACPI video notifies:

  0x86 = brightness up
  0x87 = brightness down

Volume and keyboard-backlight keys send normal extended scancodes, which
is why they already work. The Screen preferences slider and `screenmode`
also work because they use the intel_extreme accelerant path.

This folder adds a small kernel driver that installs a notify handler on
ACPI video devices (ones that implement _BCL) and publishes
/dev/power/acpi_video/0. A tiny userspace helper reads the events and
calls `screenmode -b` to step the brightness.

Not Gerrit yet. Overlay the kernel add-on and run the helper.

Build the helper with:
  gcc -o brightness-helper brightness-helper.c

Put the helper in UserBootScript or run it by hand after boot.
